  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Isaiah",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 21,
    "summary": "Babylon is fallen, is fallen!—Other nations also are destroyed.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "The burden of the desert of the sea. As whirlwinds in the south pass through; so it cometh from the desert, from a terrible land.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "IE a message or prophecy of doom to Babylon."
          },
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "OR the Negev desert."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 80
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 21:1",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "A grievous vision is declared unto me; the treacherous dealer dealeth treacherously, and the spoiler spoileth. Go up, O Elam: besiege, O Media; all the sighing thereof have I made to cease.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "Isa. 33:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 120,
            "end": 124,
            "text": "This prophecy was fulfilled in 538 B.C., about 200 years after Isaiah lived."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Isa. 33:1.",
            "prettyString": "Isaiah 33:1",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "isaiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 33,
                    "end": 33,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 1,
                        "end": 1
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 21:2",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore are my loins filled with pain: pangs have taken hold upon me, as the pangs of a woman that travaileth: I was bowed down at the hearing of it; I was dismayed at the seeing of it.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 158,
            "end": 166,
            "text": "IE Isaiah was astonished at the cataclysmic scene he saw in vision, even though an enemy was the nation destroyed."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 145,
            "end": 151
          },
          {
            "start": 181,
            "end": 187
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 21:3",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "My heart panted, fearfulness affrighted me: the night of my pleasure hath he turned into fear unto me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 21:4",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Prepare the table, watch in the watchtower, eat, drink: arise, ye princes, and anoint the shield.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 78
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 21:5",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "For thus hath the Lord said unto me, Go, set a watchman, let him declare what he seeth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "TG Preaching."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Preaching.",
            "prettyString": "TG Preaching",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Preaching",
                "entryId": "tg-preaching",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 21:6",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And he saw a chariot with a couple of horsemen, a chariot of asses, and a chariot of camels; and he hearkened diligently with much heed:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 25
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 71
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 21:7",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And he cried, A lion: My lord, I stand continually upon the watchtower in the daytime, and I am set in my ward whole nights:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 21:8",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "And, behold, here cometh a chariot of men, with a couple of horsemen. And he answered and said, Babylon is fallen, is fallen; and all the graven images of her gods he hath broken unto the ground.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 96,
            "end": 103,
            "text": "Rev. 14:8 (8–11); D&C 1:16."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 47
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 21:9",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "O my threshing, and the corn of my floor: that which I have heard of the Lord of hosts, the God of Israel, have I declared unto you.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 1,
            "text": "HEB O my threshed one and son of my threshing floor. (The prophet thus addressed the Israelites who will survive Babylon’s downfall.)"
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 21:10",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "The burden of Dumah. He calleth to me out of Seir, Watchman, what of the night? Watchman, what of the night?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "IE a message of doom to the Edomites."
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 49,
            "text": "Gen. 36:8 (8–9); Ezek. 35:2."
          },
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 78,
            "text": "IE How much is spent? How long will darkness (i.e., oppression) last?"
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 21:11",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "The watchman said, The morning cometh, and also the night: if ye will inquire, inquire ye: return, come.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "IE The end of Babylonian captivity approaches, but another oppressor follows; inquire again later."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 21:12",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "The burden upon Arabia. In the forest in Arabia shall ye lodge, O ye travelling companies of Dedanim.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "Arabian caravans and camps would also suffer disruption and oppression by the Babylonian conquest ( vv. 13–17)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 21:13",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "The inhabitants of the land of Tema brought water to him that was thirsty, they prevented with their bread him that fled.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 21:14",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "For they fled from the swords, from the drawn sword, and from the bent bow, and from the grievousness of war.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 21:15",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "For thus hath the Lord said unto me, Within a year, according to the years of an hireling, and all the glory of Kedar shall fail:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 112,
            "end": 117,
            "text": "Isa. 60:7."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Isa. 60:7.",
            "prettyString": "Isaiah 60:7",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "isaiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 60,
                    "end": 60,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 7,
                        "end": 7
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 21:16",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "And the residue of the number of archers, the mighty men of the children of Kedar, shall be diminished: for the Lord God of Israel hath spoken it.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 143,
            "end": 146
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
